    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d450da60_33683475",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityDiagnosticsManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 330,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T16:34:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The number of threads ? How can you even know this ? Executor does not expose a facility to tell you how many threads it uses. Not all Executors are instances of ThreadPoolExecutor. Even if you are passed an instance of ThreadPoolExecutor how does that work exactly ? I don\u0027t see a reasonable way of making this work.\n\nI also do not think it\u0027s reasonable at all to ask for the client to create 80 threads if they want 80 concurrent probes (which is not particularly far-fetched). Parallelism in networking is normally achieved with use of poll() when writing in C or C++, not with massive amounts of threads, for usage of resource reasons.\n\nI think you need to have the parallelism configuration in the Params object, and implement it with poll() like normal.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 327,
        "startChar": 96,
        "endLine": 330,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "03d4ee4a9121c54eb06e0e5f5a5b0b21138cac8b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
